Algebra library source tree
===========================

This directory contains the source of the Algebra library.  The former
[g]make targets were retired in modernization v0.02.

Build the library through the supported recursive build system.  Normally,
from the distribution root:

    bash build.sh build

After the compiler and prerequisite libraries have already been built, the
Algebra subtree may be rebuilt directly with:

    (cd lib/algebra && bash build.sh build)

The build.sh files encode a non-trivial dependency order, including
interleaved matrix and univariate-polynomial stages.  Preserve that order
when changing the build machinery.  Products are written below ALDORROOT.
Use the top-level `bash build.sh test` command for the supported distribution
test sequence.
